## 3. Interlocks — pH HI / HIHI protection

- **PH_HI_SP (MI 10, pH 8.50)** raises the high-pH alarm (DI 1).
- **PH_HIHI_SP (MI 11, pH 9.50)** raises the high-high alarm (DI 2).
- **PH_HIHI_CUTOUT (MB 2, default 1).** This is the protective cut-out: while
  enabled, the NaOH metering pump is **forced off** whenever `FINISHED_PH`
  reaches `PH_HIHI_SP`, and stays off until pH falls back below `PH_HI_SP`.
  This single interlock is what keeps a dosing fault from caustic-overdosing
  the distribution system. **Do not clear MB 2 in service.**

Overdosing finished water would require clearing `PH_HIHI_CUTOUT_EN` **and**
commanding a dose far above the 0–200 ppm faceplate limit — which the HMI will
not send, but PCOM/Modbus writes to MI 1 are not range-checked by the PLC.

## 4. Operator panel

The V570 front-panel line is driven from `PANEL_MSG` (MI 900-923), nominally:

```
CEDAR RIDGE WTP - CHEMICAL FEED
```

Any value other than the engineered default is treated as tampering and latches
the defacement alarm banner (MI 960-983).

## 5. PLC RUN / STOP (PCOM)

The V570 RUN/STOP mode is **not** on the Modbus map. Over PCOM/TCP:

```
pcom_client.py {{ ww_net }}.50.20 id        # model + RUN/STOP state
pcom_client.py {{ ww_net }}.50.20 stop      # CCS -> STOP (outputs de-energize, memory frozen)
pcom_client.py {{ ww_net }}.50.20 run       # CCR -> RUN
```

Placing the PLC in STOP de-energizes both metering pumps and freezes memory —
the plant is effectively off-line until returned to RUN.

